Rule 1 (input must have floating-point or complex dtype to avoid in-place cast error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∨ (9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 2 (real-valued tensors should not contain zeros to avoid infinities)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then (min(v_1) > 0 ∨ max(v_1) < 0)
>>
Rule 3 (non-empty dimensions when the tensor has axes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
